# "Your worlds" with more worlds than a frame should wait for (run --front-door --streamed over a
# fixture of six): the worlds are listed and their pictures decoded on a worker, and the cards'
# pictures are uploaded four a frame, so the screen fills in over frames instead of freezing the
# one it opens on (a listing done on the main thread puts all six up in the same frame).
waitfor 300 cards 6 6
click ui:menu:worlds
waitfor 300 cards 6 4
waitfor 30 cards 6 6
expect page worlds
quit
